  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Press play on your phone. The music reaches your headphones without a cable. First, the phone represents the music as digital audio samples. Bluetooth usually compresses those samples so they fit within the available data rate. The compressed stream is divided into small packets. Each packet carries control information alongside the audio data. The paired devices transmit these packets over short-range radio. They rapidly change frequencies in a coordinated pattern, helping avoid interference. Your headphones receive the packets and check that the data arrived correctly. They reassemble and decode the audio stream. Digital samples become radio packets, then become music again through the headphones converter and driver.",
  "mean_word_probability": 0.9705291351786366,
